A rich chocolate [[Cookbook:Cake|cake]] recipe.

==Ingredients==
=== Cake ===
*2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] (470 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]]) white [[cookbook:sugar|sugar]]
*1 ¾ cup (415 ml) [[cookbook:flour|flour]]
*1 ¾ cups (415 ml) baking [[cookbook:cocoa|cocoa]] powder
*1 ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] (7 ml) [[cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]
*1 ½ teaspoon (7 ml) [[cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]
*1 teaspoon [[cookbook:salt|salt]] (5ml)
*2 [[cookbook:egg|eggs]]
*1 cup (235 ml) [[cookbook:milk|milk]]
*½ cup (120 ml) [[cookbook:Vegetable Oil|vegetable oil]]
*2 teaspoons (10 ml) [[cookbook:Vanilla Extract|vanilla extract]]
*1 cup (235 ml) boiling [[cookbook:water|water]]

=== Frosting ===
*⅛ cup (30 ml) [[cookbook:cocoa|cocoa]]
*7 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]] (200 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) [[cookbook:Dark chocolate|dark chocolate]]
*⅛ cup (30 ml) boiling [[cookbook:water|water]]
*1/16 cup (15 ml) [[cookbook:Powdered Sugar|powdered sugar]]
*⅔ cup (156 ml) [[cookbook:Cream|whipping cream]]
== Procedure ==

=== Cake ===
#Mix the dry ingredients well in a large bowl. For better texture, sift the dry ingredients together with a sieve or sifter.
#Add the eggs, milk, vanilla, and vegetable oil, and mix well. Add the water, and mix it until it has a lot of little bubbles. This batter will be very thin.
#Pour into two greased 9-inch round [[Cookbook:Cake Pan|baking pans]].
#[[cookbook:Bake|Bake]] in a preheated [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] at 180°C for 30 minutes (about 20 minutes for a convection oven), or until a cake tester comes out clean. Remember not to over-bake the cake, as it may become really dry and lose all its moisture.
#Cool the cakes completely, then unmold them.
=== Frosting ===
#Melt the chocolate by placing it in a [[Cookbook:Double Boiler|double boiler]].
#Mix the sugar and cocoa together in a small bowl, then mix in the water.
#Stir the sugar/cocoa/water mix into the melted chocolate.
#Quickly stir in the cream and mix until it has a smooth consistency.
#Immediately 'frost' the cake with this, making sure that there is quite a bit between the two layers of cake. The cake will need to be refrigerated to harden the fudge, so don't worry about its relatively liquid nature.
#Refrigerate cake.
#Serve warm after refrigeration. To serve, slice a piece and microwave it for about 20 seconds. The fudge will melt and soak into the cake. Serve with ice cream if you so desire.

== Notes, tips, and variations ==

* Higher quality chocolate and baking cocoa will make a noticeable difference in the cake's overall quality.
* A hot fudge sauce to go over top of the cake can be a nice extra touch.
* Don't try and substitute unsweetened chocolate for the dark chocolate.
* Spices such as [[cookbook:cinnamon|cinnamon]] can be added to the frosting if desired.

